[{"text":"FCLoopGetEtaSigns[exp] is an auxiliary function that extracts the signs of \\(i \\eta\\) from propagators present in the input expression. The result is returned as a list, e.g. {}, {1}, {-1} or {-1,1}.","anchor":"fcloopgetetasigns"},{"text":"This is useful if one wants ensure that all propagators of the given integral or topology follow a particular \\(i \\eta\\) sign convention.","anchor":"fcloopgetetasigns"},{"text":"Overview, FCTopology, FCLoopSwitchEtaSign.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"FAD[{p, m}] FCLoopGetEtaSigns[%]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{p^2-m^2}\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\{1\\}\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SFAD[{p, m^2}] FCLoopGetEtaSigns[%]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(p^2-m^2+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\{1\\}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SFAD[{I p, -m^2}, EtaSign -> -1] FCLoopGetEtaSigns[%]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(-p^2+m^2-i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\{-1\\}\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CFAD[{p, m^2}] FCLoopGetEtaSigns[%]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(p^2+m^2-i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\{-1\\}\\]","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"}]